    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0616" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.534/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-22T11:00:00+01:00">July 22, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Department’s instruction 958, December 1, 1928;<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d282-f1"/> and 1029 June 27, 1929, military service in Portugal of
                    naturalized citizens of the United States.</p>
                <p>May Legation consider these instructions as dealing with two phases of same
                    situation and seek a permanent solution for both in the treaty desired by our
                    Government? If so, please draw and forward for use in negotiations draft text
                    adequately covering all points.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
